   Also the number regex: contract says numbers are "nonnegative literals: integers, decimals (1.5, .5, 5.), and optional e/E exponent with optional sign". Regex looks right. But wait — "5." — `[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]*)?` matches "5.". Good.

